execute Python.\n- Finish typed edits and scripts with **Keep changes without saving**, **Save font**, or their recovery action. Typed edits offer selective Undo; scripts offer whole-font **Restore saved version**, which discards later unsaved edits and cannot restore external effects.\n- Successful, visible result cards offer a 30-second automatic Keep countdown and **Wait for my answer**. Text-only clients remain manual.\n- Prepare width deltas, Dimensions, glyph colors and coordinate-only outlines without full-font copies or external-worker startup. Complex algorithms and exports retain their existing routes.\n- Add background-outline targeting, glyph color actions, template favorites and menus, and Setup layout improvements. Keep twelve tools, eleven managed skills and the existing 4,096 eligible-surface limit.\n\nThe desktop requires macOS 14 or later and Glyphs 4. Glyphs 3 remains on its separate v1.11.0 release. Start with disposable font copies: this is a beta, not a production-readiness claim.\n\nValidation: 2,262 Python tests passed (one skip), 210 macOS tests passed, deterministic ARM64/Intel payloads, and actual editor saving, restoration, Undo/Redo and installed Codex text workflows. The paired performance report contains 320 fresh-process runs; it does not guarantee responsiveness on other fonts or machines.\n\nKnown qualification gaps: installed visual card countdown/Details testing, physical Intel, minimum-macOS and parts of the manual client/fault-injection matrix remain open. Native unnamed-node null-to-empty normalization is a separate typed-recovery follow-up. See the release qualification and beta guide for exact scope.\n\n[Beta guide](https://github.com/thierryc/Glyphs-mcp/blob/lit/v2-beta/BETA.md) · [Qualification](https://github.com/thierryc/Glyphs-mcp/blob/lit/v2-beta/reports/beta7-release-20260927/README.md)\n\nThe signed desktop update and component migration have not been exercised on this exact release. Signing, notarization and artifact verification passed; this update-path qualification remains open.\n"}